# Curriculum Overview

## What is The Fabric of the Internet and AI about?
 
#### This unit explores how the Internet and networks function, their societal and ethical impacts, and their real-world applications. Students examine data transmission, IP addressing, DNS resolution, network security, and AI’s role in cybersecurity. Through hands-on simulations and discussions, students analyze how data moves through networks, how protocols ensure secure communication, and how issues like the digital divide affect global connectivity

#### Ethical problem-solving and collaboration help students propose solutions to improve Internet access and security. Grounded in computational thinking and real-world relevance, this unit fosters curiosity, critical thinking, and innovation, preparing students to engage with networking technologies and their societal implications.

#### **This is the fourth unit in the six unit <a href='https://code.org/en-US/curriculum/artificial-intelligence-foundations' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>AI Foundations</a> semester 1 course. This professional learning module prepares you to teach it!**

## Student Learning Goals
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold;">Students will:</h4>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      	<li>Describe how data is transmitted over the Internet.</li>
		<li>Assess the implications of the digital divide and propose strategies to promote equitable Internet access.</li>
        <li>Analyze the role of AI in enhancing network security.</li>
        <li>Propose and evaluate solutions to complex networking challenges, including security risks and accessibility issues.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
