## Classroom Context

#### This content has been developed for high school students with little or no coding experience who are comfortable with technology and curious about AI and computer science.

#### This unit can be implemented on it's own or part of the AI Foundations Semester or year-long course.

#### All lessons within the unit are intended to be facilitated by a teacher. These lessons are not designed as self-paced experiences for students to work through at their own pace.

<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;">
    ➡️ Learn more about the AI Foundations Curriculum by taking the <a href='https://studio.code.org/courses/teaching-ai-foundations-s1-v2-2025/units/1' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' style='text-decoration: none; font-weight: bold;'>Introductory Module</a>.
</p>


## Unit Length and Format



#### **Total Duration:** Approximately 3 weeks
#### **Structure:** Twelve 45-minute lessons and one 3-day culminating project
<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;">
